Use an organization-based, multi-tenant architecture. An individual family may manage a private wedding workspace, while a professional planner may manage multiple client organizations or weddings under authorized arrangements.

Each wedding must support multiple functions, venues, guest groups, vendors, budgets and staff members.

Implement granular, server-enforced role-based permissions. A vendor must only see the weddings, functions and information explicitly shared with them. Family members must not automatically gain access to other families' weddings. Platform administrators must have audited, appropriately restricted access.

