## 19. DATA INTEGRITY AND BUSINESS RULES

Establish explicit rules:
- Each guest has a stable internal identifier.
- Each guest may have separate responses for each function.
- Household size is not automatically equivalent to confirmed attendance.
- Duplicate submissions must not inflate attendance counts.
- RSVP edits must update all relevant authorized reports.
- Forecasts must never overwrite actual confirmed responses.
- Check-in counts must be based on individual attendance records.
- Catering commitments must be distinct from forecast estimates.
- Finalized headcounts require explicit authorization for changes.
- Every important change must have an attributable activity record.
- All date calculations must respect the event's timezone.
- Deleted, archived or revoked invitation records must not remain accessible through old public links.
- Financial calculations must use validated numeric inputs and documented rounding rules.

Provide reconciliation tools for imported guests, RSVP counts, check-in counts and catering invoices.

